To solve this problem, we can use polynomial long division. The given polynomial is $2x^6-x^4+4x^2-7$, and the divisor is $x^2+4x+3$. We can set up the division as follows:
\[
\begin{array}{c|ccccc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{2x^4} & -8x^3 & +16x^2 & -12x & +20 \\
\cline{2-6}
x^2+4x+3 & 2x^6 & -x^4 & +4x^2 & -7 & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{2x^6} & +8x^5 & +6x^4 \\ 
\cline{2-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0} & -8x^5 & -7x^4 & +3x^3 & +12x^2 \\ 
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & -8x^5 & -32x^4 & -24x^3 \\ 
\cline{3-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 0 & 25x^4 & 27x^3 & -6x^2 & +12x^2 \\ 
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 25x^4 & +100x^3 & +75x^2 \\ 
\cline{4-6}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 0 & -73x^3 & -81x^2 & +107x & -7 \\ 
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & -73x^3 & -292x^2 & -219x \\ 
\cline{5-7}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 0 & 211x^2 & 107x & -226 \\ 
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & & 211x^2 & +844x & +633 \\ 
\cline{6-8}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & & 0 & 737x & +407 \\ 
\end{array}
\end{array}
\]
The remainder is $20$. </answer>

